    "title": "Northwestern College will soon see construction - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Reilly Mahon Maren Ewertz ,\n1 hours ago\nORANGE CITY , Iowa ( KCAU ) — One northwest Iowa higher institution will begin a construction project for a plaza near its football and track stadium.\nNorthwestern College officials said Colenbrander Plaza will be an outdoor gathering space close to De Valois Stadium.\nStory continues below\nThe plaza will be located where Colenbrander Hall once stood from 1960 until 2024.\nOfficials said Colenbrander Plaza will feature seat walls, brick pillars, and a big athletic logo.\nA public groundbreaking is set for October 2 at 5 p.m.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
